  ('916551821696062989', 'The Golden Bowl', 2000, 'Romance, Drama', 'James Ivory, Tony Pierce-Roberts', 'Ruth Prawer Jhabvala', 'Kate Beckinsale, Uma Thurman, Jeremy Northam, Nick Nolte, Anjelica Huston, James Fox, Madeleine Potter, Nicholas Day', 'R', 'Wealthy American widower Adam Verver and his daughter Maggie live a refined life in Europe, surrounded by art. Maggie marries impoverished Italian Prince Amerigo, while Adam marries Maggie''s friend Charlotte Stant. The Prince and Charlotte are having an affair, which Maggie discovers and navigates through a silent, psychological battle of wills, ultimately using her cunning to preserve her marriage and protect her father.', 'Wealthy American widower Adam Verver and his daughter Maggie live a refined life in Europe, surrounded by art. Maggie marries impoverished Italian Prince Amerigo, while Adam marries Maggie''s friend Charlotte Stant. The Prince and Charlotte are having an affair, which Maggie discovers and navigates through a silent, psychological battle of wills, ultimately using her cunning to preserve her marriage and protect her father.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/xgUcUWu7lirlZbMPz21qo8RhK57.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:29946'),
