  ('820797685061707039', 'The Great Rock ''n'' Roll Swindle', 1980, 'Comedy, Documentary, Music', 'Julien Temple, Willi Patterson, John Metcalfe', 'Julien Temple', 'Malcolm McLaren, Steve Jones, Paul Cook, Sid Vicious, John Lydon, Helen Wellington-Lloyd, Ronald Biggs, Liz Fraser', null, 'A rather incoherent post-breakup Sex Pistols "documentary", told from the point of view of Pistols manager Malcolm McLaren, whose (arguable) position is that the Sex Pistols in particular and punk rock in general were an elaborate scam perpetrated by him in order to make "a million pounds."', 'A rather incoherent post-breakup Sex Pistols "documentary", told from the point of view of Pistols manager Malcolm McLaren, whose (arguable) position is that the Sex Pistols in particular and punk rock in general were an elaborate scam perpetrated by him in order to make "a million pounds."', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/A8Q8rhuv8YszuFuYrsCAo9281mt.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:16149'),
  ('997181867530242504', 'The Great Rupert', 1950, 'Family, Comedy', 'Irving Pichel, Harold Godsoe, Lionel Lindon', 'Harry Crane, James O''Hanlon', 'Jimmy Durante, Terry Moore, Tom Drake, Frank Orth, Sara Haden, Queenie Smith, Chick Chandler, Jimmy Conlin', 'NR', 'Shortly before Christmas, a family moves into an apartment where Rupert the squirrel lives in the attic rafters. Just as it seems that the holiday will come and go without so much as a Christmas tree, Rupert acts as the family''s guardian angel - not only saving Christmas, but changing their lives forever.', 'Shortly before Christmas, a family moves into an apartment where Rupert the squirrel lives in the attic rafters. Just as it seems that the holiday will come and go without so much as a Christmas tree, Rupert acts as the family''s guardian angel - not only saving Christmas, but changing their lives forever.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/aJGIPdcB8JddD3gpCTEIN9j6K1O.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:50926'),
  ('950889349810104347', 'The Great Sacrifice', 1944, 'Drama, Romance', 'Veit Harlan', 'Alfred Braun, Veit Harlan, Hans Radtke', 'Carl Raddatz, Irene von Meyendorff, Kristina Söderbaum, Franz Schafheitlin, Ernst Stahl-Nachbaur, Paul Bildt, Otto Treßler, Annemarie Steinsieck', null, 'Äls, a young woman from Sweden living in Hamburg in the summer months attracts a newly married explorer, Albrecht Froben who has just returned to his native city. But although Äls seems to be ''life itself'', she suffers from a tropical disease which is slowly killing her. Froben is torn between Äls and his wife Octavia, who he seen as a kind of ''heavenly'' counterpart to the earthy and beguiling Äls.', 'Äls, a young woman from Sweden living in Hamburg in the summer months attracts a newly married explorer, Albrecht Froben who has just returned to his native city. But although Äls seems to be ''life itself'', she suffers from a tropical disease which is slowly killing her. Froben is torn between Äls and his wife Octavia, who he seen as a kind of ''heavenly'' counterpart to the earthy and beguiling Äls.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/As23kcxBPVu5Mr6inaWwVBBsizn.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:97088'),
  ('232992534279397218', 'The Great Santini', 1979, 'Drama', 'Lewis John Carlino, Ralph Woolsey', 'Lewis John Carlino', 'Robert Duvall, Blythe Danner, Michael O''Keefe, Lisa Jane Persky, Julie Anne Haddock, Brian Andrews, Stan Shaw, Theresa Merritt', 'PG', 'As he approaches manhood, Ben Meechum struggles to win the approval of his demanding alpha male father, an aggressively competitive, but frustrated marine pilot.', 'As he approaches manhood, Ben Meechum struggles to win the approval of his demanding alpha male father, an aggressively competitive, but frustrated marine pilot.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/xvoHFQlSAq0696rvONsEAWj1fcm.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:21887'),
  ('49981352907668641', 'The Great Scout & Cathouse Thursday', 1976, 'Comedy, Western', 'Álex Phillips Jr., Don Taylor', 'Richard Alan Shapiro', 'Lee Marvin, Oliver Reed, Robert Culp, Elizabeth Ashley, Strother Martin, Sylvia Miles, Kay Lenz, Howard Platt', 'PG', 'Sam Longwood, a frontiersman who has seen better days, spies the gold-mine partner, Jack Colby, who ran off with all the gold from a mine they were prospecting fifteen years earlier. He tells his other partners from that time, Joe Knox and Billy, and they confront Colby demanding not only the thousand dollars he took but an addition fifty-nine thousand for their trouble. After being thwarted in this attempt, they, and a would-be named Thursday, hatch a plan to kidnap Colby''s wife, Nancy Sue, who is coincidently Sam''s old flame, but find that Nancy Sue is not the sweet girl that Sam remembers.', 'Sam Longwood, a frontiersman who has seen better days, spies the gold-mine partner, Jack Colby, who ran off with all the gold from a mine they were prospecting fifteen years earlier. He tells his other partners from that time, Joe Knox and Billy, and they confront Colby demanding not only the thousand dollars he took but an addition fifty-nine thousand for their trouble. After being thwarted in this attempt, they, and a would-be named Thursday, hatch a plan to kidnap Colby''s wife, Nancy Sue, who is coincidently Sam''s old flame, but find that Nancy Sue is not the sweet girl that Sam remembers.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/1qiDqaJEUc2mCqErJ5V7N40mgoN.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:50953'),
