  ('505560016829460356', 'The Guardsman', 1931, 'Comedy, Drama', 'Sidney Franklin, Harold S. Bucquet, Douglas Shearer', 'Ernest Vajda', 'Alfred Lunt, Lynn Fontanne, Roland Young, Zasu Pitts, Maude Eburne, Herman Bing, Ann Dvorak, Geraldine Dvorak', 'NR', 'An acclaimed actor and his equally acclaimed actress wife, who have been married for less than a year, are already showing signs of strain in their marriage. The actor believes his wife is capable of infidelity and sets out to prove this is so. Disguising himself as the kind of man he believes she fancies (a Russian military officer), the actor woos his wife while she believes her husband to be out of town.', 'An acclaimed actor and his equally acclaimed actress wife, who have been married for less than a year, are already showing signs of strain in their marriage. The actor believes his wife is capable of infidelity and sets out to prove this is so. Disguising himself as the kind of man he believes she fancies (a Russian military officer), the actor woos his wife while she believes her husband to be out of town.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/qFCg6EJPLidIgwwolbwLBb42qEG.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:95004'),
  ('130097744955903581', 'The Guernsey Literary & Potato Peel Pie Society', 2018, 'Romance, Drama, History', 'Mike Newell, Zac Nicholson, Jack Ravenscroft', 'Don Roos, Thomas Bezucha, Kevin Hood', 'Lily James, Jessica Brown Findlay, Matthew Goode, Michiel Huisman, Katherine Parkinson, Glen Powell, Tom Courtenay, Kit Connor', null, 'Free-spirited writer Juliet Ashton forms a life-changing bond with the delightful and eccentric Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society, when she decides to write about the book club they formed during the occupation of Guernsey in WWII.', 'Free-spirited writer Juliet Ashton forms a life-changing bond with the delightful and eccentric Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society, when she decides to write about the book club they formed during the occupation of Guernsey in WWII.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/55oz5d6NdH7ohbM1I1Euh1Tt6PN.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:451480'),
  ('1054191754017431008', 'The Guest', 2014, 'Mystery, Thriller, Action', 'Adam Wingard, Robby Baumgartner', 'Simon Barrett', 'Dan Stevens, Maika Monroe, Brendan Meyer, Sheila Kelley, Leland Orser, Lance Reddick, Joel David Moore, Ethan Embry', 'R', 'A soldier introduces himself to the Peterson family, claiming to be a friend of their son who died in action. After the young man is welcomed into their home, a series of accidental deaths seem to be connected to his presence.', 'A soldier introduces himself to the Peterson family, claiming to be a friend of their son who died in action. After the young man is welcomed into their home, a series of accidental deaths seem to be connected to his presence.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/gvlEFHu9FuYLmBZwsARTtuNIiDO.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:241848'),
